-- check/good: §10.9 and A.83. The warning about an unannotated `pub`
-- declaration whose inferred scheme carries a constraint is emitted by
-- DEFAULT — the walker runs plain `beni check`, with no `--explain` — and it
-- is a `warning`, so the fixture still exits 0 and still has an `.iface`.
--
-- `annotated` is the twin that pins its type. An annotation's `where` clause
-- is the whole set (Rule U2), so it promotes nothing and says nothing: the
-- `.diag` golden names `bigger` and never `annotated`, which is the hint the
-- message gives.
pub bigger a b = a < b


pub annotated : Int, Int -> Bool
annotated a b = a < b
